          <caption>
            <p>Archimedes Principle. Any given mass will displace a volume of water equal to its submerged volume.&#x0202d; &#x0202c;To float,&#x0202d; an object's upward buoyant force must exceed the gravitational downward force.&#x0202d; Pbrks, <ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Buoyancy.svg">Public Domain</ext-link>, via Wikimedia Commons</p>
